From 7aa2ec350cedd0427a19cd7b17526fb8d0468669 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Lamb <paul@paulscode.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 04:36:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Issue an offer invoice with a path from this node when no
 peer can start one

An invoice's blinded payment paths are found through the node's peers, and
a peer is only used as an introduction node when it has a channel other
than the one to this node. On a small chain that is often not so: a node
whose only peer's only channel is the one between them could mint an offer
but answered every invoice request with "cannot issue an invoice right
now", so a pool could not pay it.

When the node's settings ask for a path through a peer and none is found,
the offer server now asks again for a path that starts at this node, which
always exists, padded with dummy hops as the settings say. The payer then
learns the node id, which an offer without paths shows anyway, and the
invoice is issued. The fallback is logged.

(cherry picked from commit abeb95686ff9ef57adfa5a96dc22b53600820550)
